BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:FIKR: Talks Over Tea
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260916T170000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260916T190000
DTSTAMP:20260905T130953Z
UID:dartmouth-groups-1631521@free-food-dartmouth
SEQUENCE:0
CLASS:PUBLIC
DESCRIPTION:Original event page(s):\nhttps://dartmouthgroups.dartmouth.edu
 /rsvp_boot?id=1631521\n\nDescription:\nThis Fall\, we are launching a new 
 initiative: FIKR at Dartmouth — Fellowship for Islamic Knowledge and Ref
 lection.\nFIKR is built around a simple idea: before asking students to pr
 oduce thoughtful writing\, we should first create opportunities for them t
 o read\, encounter\, question\, and think thoughtfully together. Throughou
 t the Fall\, our programming will include an Omar Ibn Said book fellowship
 \, an in-person guest lecture\, and a weekly series called FIKR: Talks Ove
 r Tea. The questions and conversations that emerge from these experiences 
 will then help shape the Journal’s inaugural Winter publication.\nFor We
 ek 1 of FIKR: Talks Over Tea\, our opening conversation is: What Is Knowle
 dge For? Faith\, Learning\, and Unlearning at College\nWe hope to explore 
 questions such as: Why are we actually in college? Is knowledge primarily 
 for career and achievement\, or should it transform who we become? What ma
 kes seeking knowledge meaningful in Islam? Can someone become more educate
 d while becoming less wise? How should Muslims approach ideas that genuine
 ly challenge what they already believe?\nBefore the gathering\, we plan to
  give students a short excerpt from al-Ghazali’s Book of Knowledge on in
 tention and the purpose of learning\, with Malcolm X’s “Learning to Re
 ad” as an optional accompanying text.\nProfessor Ayubi will join us as o
 ur first guest speaker.\nFood Provided (Persian saffron tea with cinnamon 
 and Pakistiani Chai)\n\nSponsor / organizer: The Dartmouth Undergraduate M
 uslim Journal\n\nSource: Dartmouth Groups\n\nWhy this was included: Free F
 ood category\; explicit food-service wording\; food or meal keyword in tit
 le\n\nFood availability is inferred from the source listing\; verify detai
 ls before attending.
LAST-MODIFIED:20260905T130953Z
LOCATION:Private Location (register to display)
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
URL:https://dartmouthgroups.dartmouth.edu/rsvp_boot?id=1631521
X-MICROSOFT-CDO-BUSYSTATUS:FREE
END:VEVENT
