BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:HOOD SALON INFO SESSION
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260917T121500
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260917T131500
DTSTAMP:20260905T130953Z
UID:dartmouth-82568@free-food-dartmouth
SEQUENCE:0
CLASS:PUBLIC
DESCRIPTION:Original event page(s):\nhttps://home.dartmouth.edu/events/eve
 nt?event=82568\nhttps://hoodmuseum.dartmouth.edu/explore/exhibitions/commu
 nity-and-exile\nhttps://hoodmuseum.dartmouth.edu/learn/college-students\n\
 nDescription:\nJoin exhibition curator Elizabeth Rice Mattison in\nCommun
 ity and Exile: Artists in Paris\, 1910–1939\nto learn more about the up
 coming Hood Salon! Coffee and snacks will be provided.\nThe exhibition fea
 tures work from the Hood Museum’s collection by immigrant artists who so
 ught refuge in Paris\, from the beginning of the 20th century until World 
 War II. Artists came to the city to escape persecution\, societal strictu
 res\, and economic stagnation elsewhere in the world. Paris allowed them 
 to build a community in their new home and to forge a thriving\, interdisc
 iplinary cultural scene.\nIn the same spirit of creative and cultural exch
 ange\, the museum is welcoming submissions from current Dartmouth graduat
 e and undergraduate students of works that respond to or expand upon 
 the themes and/or artworks in the exhibition. Selected works will be repr
 oduced in a publication made available to gallery visitors within the exh
 ibition. For more information about the Hood Salon\,\nclick here\n.\n\nSpo
 nsor / organizer: Hood Museum of Art\n\nAudience: Public\n\nSource: Dartmo
 uth\n\nWhy this was included: Free Food category\; explicit food-service w
 ording\; food keyword near service context\n\nFood availability is inferre
 d from the source listing\; verify details before attending.
LAST-MODIFIED:20260905T130953Z
LOCATION:Hood Museum of Art
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
